Subject: [PATCH] phy: rockchip: allow fixed-peripheral USBDP BVALID override

The RK3588 USBDP driver normally asserts the USB BVALID override from
the Type-C orientation-switch callback. A board-specific fixed peripheral
route can use the same USBDP/USB2 GRF path without having a Type-C
orientation event, leaving the hardware BVALID override disabled.

Add an opt-in property for that fixed-routing case. Reject it when Type-C
orientation or mode switching is present so normal Type-C behaviour cannot
be overridden accidentally.

Normal device trees are unchanged when the property is absent.

--- a/drivers/phy/rockchip/phy-rockchip-usbdp.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/rockchip/phy-rockchip-usbdp.c
@@ -1497,6 +1497,16 @@
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
+	if (device_property_present(dev, "rockchip,fixed-peripheral-bvalid")) {
+		if (device_property_present(dev, "orientation-switch") ||
+		    device_property_present(dev, "mode-switch"))
+			return dev_err_probe(dev, -EINVAL,
+					     "fixed peripheral BVALID conflicts with Type-C switching\n");
+
+		rk_udphy_usb_bvalid_enable(udphy, true);
+		dev_info(dev, "forcing USB BVALID for fixed peripheral routing\n");
+	}
+
 	mutex_init(&udphy->mutex);
 	platform_set_drvdata(pdev, udphy);
 
